  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An old-fashioned bicycle is moving with a constant speed v. The front wheel has a radius 3 times that of the rear wheel. Points X and Y are positioned on the front and rear wheel as shown.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p><sup>[Source: Clu, n.d. Penny farthing bicycle. [image online] Available at:</sup><sup> </sup><sup>https://www.gettyimages.co.uk/detail/illustration/</sup><sup>penny-farthing-bicycle-first-exercise-royalty-free-illustration/1179950344</sup><sup> </sup><sup>[Accessed 16 May 2023]. Source</sup> <sup>adapted.]</sup></p>\n<p>What is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\textit{acceleration of X}}{\\textit{acceleration of Y}}\"></span> ?<br/><br/></p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{9}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{3}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\">3</li><li data-label=\"D\">9</li></ol>"
